# Terminates TLS with Caddy's self-signed internal CA so Mastonet's hardcoded "https://" has something to land on.
# The site address names the host rather than being left bare (":443"): "tls internal" provisions a certificate for
# whatever the address names at startup, and a bare port gives it nothing to provision one for — Caddy then has no
# certificate to answer a "localhost" ClientHello with and the handshake fails with "no certificate available". The
# port a test dials (127.0.0.1:34443, mapped in docker-compose.yml) is outside this file's business — Caddy only
# needs to know what it listens on inside the container.
localhost:443 {
	tls internal

	reverse_proxy web:3000
}
